Z||000000||Haspers8||05-05-2001||12:14 PM||||I went to Racecity Speedway in Calgary Alberta to try some drag racing.  So here is the best time with my car.<P>   R/T     0.649<BR>   60‘     1.943<BR>   1/8     8.702 at 78.76mph.<BR>   1000   11.420<BR>   1/4    13.718 at 97.68mph.<P>-85 se4spd converted to 95 LT-1 with 5spd<BR>-Wingless Imsa, on 16‘s with adj Konis.<P>Later<BR>Steve||||reg||6
Z||000001||88formula||05-05-2001||04:13 PM||||Someone who says they have lots of track experience told me when I posted a 13.8 quarter mile and 98 mph from my Dragstrip2000 program that these times don't mix. He implied that the mph was to low and that I would have to do some perfect driving to get those times. Well here it is. Proof that this is possible, thanks. <P>Good times by the way. I like it. I bet that time was traction limited. What launch rpm did you launch with and what RPM did you shift at? <P><BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 05-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||pontiacs4me||05-05-2001||04:28 PM||||Kind of like my firebird, I run around 14.60 at 99-100 mph. It lauches real slow because of the 3.08 gears, but comes on real strong in the last 1/8th.  My friend tom has a 91 lumina with a 3800 supercharged, and a 70 shot of NOS.  He runs 13.20 at 110 mph.  Thats enough mph for a 12.70.  It all depends on the launch.  My best 60 foot was a 2.28. Ive never ran my fiero, yet.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Haspers8||05-05-2001||08:25 PM||||   Well I am trying to find a scanner so I can post the slip.   The competion is called Secret Street.  Everything from Toyota 4runners to 9sec pros.  The Fiero sure was a hit though,  talked to a lot of people and I am sure Archie is going to have a few phone calls from Calgary...hehe.  <P>It was the first time I had ever raced so.....ya I will try better next time, sure was fun though.  I made 7 passes in all, some good some bad.  Can you say 1.2 sec reaction time.  Two with a blown 3 to 4 shift. Leon a guy with a 13 sec turbo daytona said I should  leave on the last yellow...helped alot.  <BR>  On my last 3 passes I was having some trouble with misfire but hopefully I can have that worked out by next friday.<P>  Don‘t really know shift points or what I was running when I left the line...to scared to look at anything but the track.  One guy said he was sure there was air under the front tires on one launch.  The waterbox was not much fun either, car just bounced. Bushing problem maybe.... Koni‘s on the front were set to full soft as was the rear.<P>But hey if you have never tried it, go for it.  Much fun!!!!!!<BR>later <BR>Steve<BR>PS anybody know where I could find an IMSA wing....||||reg||1
